2101O'Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
Re: Nationway Reconstruction Project
Dear Mr.Cobb,
Thank you so much for considering Western Research and Development, Ltd.(Westerm)for the design
work on this project.I have attached to thisletter a detailed scope of work(Exhibit B)for the Nation way
Reconstruction Project in addition to the summary below.
1.Western will be responsible for the design of the intersection at Nationway/12h Street/Ridge
Road.Said intersection will be defined as approximately 100feet to the east of the intersection
on12Street, approximately100feet north and south on Ridge Road, and approximately300
feet west on Nationway or a distance farenough to remove the existing“oiled”base material and
Standards.
2.Western will be responsible for mitigation of the drainage issue for said intersection.Western
will design appropriate drainage infrastructure to relieve thehigh-water problem that is affecting
the asphalt at this intersection.
3.Western will incorporate into the plan set the drawings for the mill and overlay for the section of
road from Logan Avenue to said intersection along Nationway and from said intersection on
Ridge Road to College Drive.Said drawings and liability for the mill and overlay will be
stampedby the City Engineer and be the responsibility of the City of Cheyenne.
4.Western will add in two days of drafting time that may be required by the City of Cheyenne for
miscellaneous work not associated with said intersection.
5.Western will accomplish a complete redesign of the signals associated with said intersection
which will be tied into the existing City system.
6.Western will use the same configuration for the lanes as exists currently.
7.Western will upgrade and redesign any sidewalks, ADA ramps, and entrances affected by the
signal redesign for said intersection.
8.Western will work with BOPU to design and upgrade the existing waterline that crosses said
intersection to the limits stated in item 1 above.
9.All other utilities willremain as existing and no redesign is incorporated into said scope of work.
10.All changes to the above scope and or to the detailed scope attached will constitute a formal
change order for time and design fee.
